Z||000011||GodSend||02-26-2001||10:41 PM||||Hrmm.. I was hoping to bring her out on "weekend" duty starting mod/late march.. and then ease her into full duty in mid april.  Its not really the snow , its the salt I don't want to deal with.  <P> I have kept myself busy with a Stereo install over the winter.  Its going to sound real nice, heres a preview<P>1 Clarion DRK8792z Cd Deck<BR>2 Rockford Fosgate 2.9x amps - one behind each seat, lower fire wall.  Mounted on seperate amp racks.<BR>1 Image Dynamics 10" IDQ sub Woofer located in teh arm rest. ....   This is the beauty.  I made a mold of the current center console using fiberglass, then I brought the rear section (the vertical section) forward about 5 inchs).  I also moved the computer beside one of my amps).  The new center console is essentially a "covering" which will mount over a .75" MDF sub box (located when the cpu was)..  this is finished in Gray Vinal (as is the amp racks).<P>2 DEi Studeo Nedymuim 3 way components (1' tweet, 5.25' , & 8" midbass).  These will be installed in custom door pods.  The neodymium series by Dei has a very shallow mounting depth, and should work great.<P>  I will keep you guys posted.  I have spent about 10-12 hours a week on this install for the past 2 months, its going to be wild!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||14
